      "evidence_source": "A highly significant Bartlett's test of sphericity (2 = 1437.80, df = 45, p < .001) and a Kaiser\u2014Meyer\u2013Olkin (KMO) value of .93 indicated that the BAS-2 data had adequate factorability. The results of the factor analysis indicated that only a single factor should be extracted. This factor had an eigenvalue of 5.69 and explained 56.89% of the total variance. All 10 items of the BAS-2 loaded onto this single factor and exhibited factor loadings that were fair to excellent (Table 1 displays the item-factor loadings and corresponding Arabic translation for each of the items).",
